\section{Geodesic Equations}

The geodesic equation is:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d^2 x^\mu}{d\lambda^2}
    + \Gamma^\mu_{\alpha\beta}
    \frac{dx^\alpha}{d\lambda}
    \frac{dx^\beta}{d\lambda}
    = 0.
\end{equation}

\section{First-Order Reduction}

Define $u^\mu = dx^\mu/d\lambda$. Then:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d}{d\lambda}
    \begin{pmatrix}
        x^\mu \\ u^\mu
    \end{pmatrix}
    =
    \begin{pmatrix}
        u^\mu \\
        -\Gamma^\mu_{\alpha\beta}u^\alpha u^\beta
    \end{pmatrix}.
\end{equation}

\section{RKF89 Adaptive Integration}

An embedded 8th/9th-order Runge–Kutta–Fehlberg scheme ensures:
\begin{equation}
    \Delta x^\mu / x^\mu < 10^{-16}.
\end{equation}